meta { title = Types and records, order = 5, group = Learn }

Kalandra checks known types and infers many expression results. Ordinary unresolved or dynamic values can remain Any; they are not proof of type safety and are not accepted across a parallel boundary.

h2 { Declare structured data }

A type declaration describes a record. Here Point has two Number fields. Calling Point constructs an instance, and a dot selects a field.

The params decorator declares the function parameter types. returns declares its result type. check adds runtime checks to the decorated function. Static analysis still checks known mismatches before execution.

{{example:types}}

h2 { Worker-safe types }

Number retains floating-point behavior. When sent through Sia it uses an eight-byte float64 codec, preserving fractional values, negative zero, NaN and infinities.

The worker protocol also supports strings, booleans, null/void, recursively typed arrays, supported declared records, and finite supported unions. Arbitrary JavaScript objects, functions, unresolved promises and Any cannot cross the compiled parallel boundary. A return annotation cannot hide an unknown function body result.

Explicitly typed module data can be captured by a worker task as a snapshot. That does not serialize an arbitrary closure or make mutations shared.

